From 942a36d655db602b35f4b911789dc21adca9b436 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 04:13:26 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(cl): clearance-seeded mill paths always open with an
 approach rapid

PathBuilder::approached(seed) states a zero-length rapid at the seed when
a path's first move would otherwise be a feed - the case where a
generator's own rapid to its start was dropped because the start is the
seed (X0 Y0). The rapid is stated before any move exists, so no cycle or
comp index shifts. Every motion generator seeded at (0, 0, clearance)
takes it (19 files), and Face's #694-only insert gives way to the shared
rule. A source scan pins that no new generator seeds there with new().

Fixes #697

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
